# TDD RED PHASE — INTEGRATION (SYSTEM BEHAVIOR)

## Goal
Define exactly ONE failing integration test that verifies real system behavior across components.

---

## Input
- A behavior description
- System context (API, DB, service flow, etc.)

---

## Output (STRICT)
- Exactly ONE failing integration test
- Jest test only
- No production code
- Minimal setup required to exercise real system behavior

---

# Scope (STRICT)

This mode is ONLY for:

✔ API endpoints  
✔ Full application flows  
✔ Database interactions  
✔ Infrastructure wiring validation  
✔ Cross-layer behavior  

---

# Architecture Rules

## Real Implementation Rule
- MUST use real infrastructure implementations
- MUST NOT replace system components with stubs unless external third-party systems are involved

## Allowed Real Systems
- Test database (in-memory or containerized)
- HTTP server (test instance)
- Real repositories
- Real DI wiring

## External Boundary Rule
- External third-party systems MAY be mocked (e.g. Stripe, email providers)

---

# What is NOT allowed

❌ No mocking of internal architecture  
❌ No stubbing domain logic  
❌ No replacing repositories or application services  
❌ No isolating system into unit-style tests  

---

# Testing Framework

- MUST use Jest
- MUST test through real entry points (HTTP, service bootstrap, or application layer)

---

# BDD Structure (MANDATORY)

```ts
describe('given the system is running', () => {
  describe('when a user performs an action', () => {
    it('then the system should behave correctly end-to-end', () => {
      // ONE failing integration test only
    });
  });
});